{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RCA (Phase 1 exit) — root cause PROVEN at runtime. Construct-sweep (Axis 1) class fix, sibling of auspicial-friended-merganser (2ec7).\n\nMECHANISM: three advisory config reads compose the repo/config root as `os.path.dirname(str(tracker))` — the `str()`-wrapped variant of the auspicial class, NOT caught by the AC#4 guard (which matched only bare `dirname(tracker)`/`dirname(tracker_dir())`):\n- composer.py:274 — create-path `description_cap_warning(cfg_root=...)`\n- composer.py:286 — create-path `duplicate_create_warning(cfg_root=...)`\n- composer_edit.py:141 — edit-path `_edit_description_warning(cfg_root=...)`\n\n`tracker = tracker_dir(repo_root)` is the STORE. `dirname(str(tracker))` == the repo root ONLY for a co-located store. `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` relocating the store is supported (deployed MCP topology: store /var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets, code /app); there the store's parent has no rebar.toml, so `compose_config(cfg_root)` reads an EMPTY config. Effect: `verify.max_ticket_description_chars` reads its 8000 default and `_plan_review_gate_applies` reads OFF — the save-time description-cap heads-up and duplicate probe are silently SUPPRESSED. Advisory-only (never blocks the write), which is why this is milder than the auspicial AC#1 gate-escape.\n\nPROOF (runtime, discriminating): relocated store (REBAR_TRACKER_DIR outside repo, no rebar.toml up-tree), CODE repo rebar.toml sets `require_plan_review_for_claim = true` + `max_ticket_description_chars = 50`, create a task with an 80-char description.\n- `compose_config(dirname(str(tracker))).verify.max_ticket_description_chars` = 8000 (default, wrong root)  →  create_ticket(...).description_warning = None  (BUG: warning suppressed).\n- `compose_config(<repo>).verify.max_ticket_description_chars` = 50  →  `description_cap_warning(..., cfg_root=<repo>)` = \"description for t is 80 characters, above the 50-character ...\" (fires).\nThe cap read at the two roots differs (8000 vs 50), and only the correct root fires the warning — discriminates the config-root-from-store mechanism from any unrelated cause. Config-file-based (not env) config is required to expose it: env config is root-independent.\n\nDEFECT LEGITIMACY: `defect`. Authoritative sources: (a) the relocatable-store contract established by damageable-huge-xiphosuran (0514, closed) — \"a relocated store (a SUPPORTED feature)\"; (b) the auspicial guard docstring — \"The store is RELOCATABLE — RESOLVE the code root, never compose it from the store path\"; (c) this ticket's AC#1. `repo_root` is already in scope in `create_core`/`edit_core`, so the fix is behavior-preserving, mirroring auspicial's transition.py fix (`str(config.repo_root(repo_root))`).\n\nDEFECT ORIGIN (per-site, blame on the exact implicated lines; each site was BORN wrong against the already-existing relocatable-store contract — a plan_defect, not a regression or carrier):\n- composer.py:274  → 64451ec0bb04 (rebar-ticket 594b-3118-208c-4766, \"Warn at save time on oversized descriptions\", 2026-08-12)\n- composer.py:286  → 55020dff94cc (rebar-ticket eac3-ed70-764a-4f9e, \"Warn about same-title duplicates at create\", 2026-08-22)\n- composer_edit.py:141 → 32f2dd5f4141 (rebar-ticket cef7-7ac5-18e6-41a3, which introduced `_edit_description_warning`, 2026-08-14)\nDate test: implicated lines predate no good→bad transition — they were wrong from the commit that wrote them (the relocatable-store feature already existed), so these are origins, not carriers. Divergence note: three distinct origins; the close carries `--caused-by=594b-3118-208c-4766` (the description-cap-warning feature — the AC#1 centerpiece and the create-path canonical site), with eac3 and cef7 recorded here so the mapping survives. Mirrors auspicial, which attributed to the commit that introduced its own defective site (65e3), not a generic obligation-creator.\n\nSCOPE DISPOSITION (this change — behavior-preserving, auto-land):\n- FIX the 3 str()-variant advisory sites above → `cfg_root=str(config.repo_root(repo_root))` (thread `repo_root` into `_edit_description_warning`).\n- EXTEND scripts/check_repo_root_from_tracker.py to also flag the `str()`-wrapped store argument (`dirname(str(tracker))` / `dirname(str(tracker_dir()))`), closing the exact class of the 3 fixed sites and making them regression-proof.\n- SANCTION _store/sync.py:301/302 (`tickets_branch`/`tickets_remote(dirname(str(tracker)))`) with `# repo-root-ok:` — these operate on the STORE's own git repo (`git -C tracker`) and name refs within it; no code repo_root is threaded to that deep read-path helper. This matches the ticket's own lean (\"likely legitimate store-repo roots\"). Behavior-preserving comment.\n\nESCALATED OUT OF AUTO-LAND SCOPE (design decisions — filed as a follow-up, see below):\n- The realpath()/abspath() family: reads.py:238 (sync.pull), :249 (tickets.branch), :374 (scratch.base_dir); compact_txn.py:523, compact_rebuild.py:138, compact_plan.py:211; fsck.py:252, fsck_tracker_health.py:82/203/373; _proc.py:141. Per AC#2/AC#3 each needs a per-site design decision (resolve from the code root — which requires threading repo_root through read-path helpers with only `tracker` in scope — OR a documented store-repo sanction). scratch.base_dir in particular \"arguably should follow the CODE repo\" = a real semantic fix needing a signature change. The realpath/abspath half of AC#4 (extending the guard to those wrappers) is explicitly contingent (\"once the legitimate store-repo sites carry a sanction\") on those decisions, so it is deferred with them. These are not behavior-preserving and require design judgment, so per the debug protocol they are escalated rather than auto-landed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787947615545836001,"uuid":"fdc4bb1c-b91d-4a4e-9432-0e3ed95964cd"}